\subsection{PDF structure and parsing}{

Each WCO HS nomenclature PDF uses a two-column layout (a "Heading" column
for 4-digit codes and an "H.S. Code" column for 6-digit codes). Descriptions
appear at three indentation levels:
\itemize{
\item \strong{hs4-level} — no dash prefix; appears next to the 4-digit heading code
(e.g. \verb{03.01   Live fish.}). Establishes \code{hs4_desc} for all codes beneath
it and resets \code{hs5_desc} to \code{NA}.
\item \strong{hs5-level} — prefixed by \verb{- } (single dash) on a standalone line with
no 6-digit code; acts as a group heading for the hs6 codes below it.
Stored in \code{hs5_desc} for all subsequent codes until the next group heading
or new hs4 heading.
\item \strong{hs6-level} — appears on the same line as the 6-digit code; prefixed by
either \verb{-- } (double dash, subdivided heading) or \verb{- } (single dash, leaf
with no deeper subdivision).
}
