\subsection{Two roles of single-dash lines}{

A single-dash line plays one of two structural roles determined by whether a
6-digit code appears on the same line:
\itemize{
\item \strong{Code present} — the \code{-} text is the hs6-level description for that code.
\code{hs5_desc} is inherited from the nearest preceding standalone group heading
(or \code{NA} if none). \code{cur_hs5_desc} is not changed.
\item \strong{No code (standalone group heading)} — the \code{-} text becomes \code{hs5_desc}
for all subsequent codes until the next group heading or hs4 heading.
}
